## Knowledge Base (lore)

**First reply in a new session:** after reading CONTEXT (below), include the line `📚 lore loaded` so the human can see lore is active. Cursor hooks may inject CONTEXT silently; do not skip the visible signal.

On session start:
1. Read `.pi/kb/CONTEXT.md` if present (or use injected CONTEXT if already in context)
2. If it references `@workspace` / `.pikb`, read workspace `.pikb/MAP.md` (first ~80 lines)
3. Run `~/.agents/skills/lore/scripts/on-session-start.sh` when unsure about KB health

During work:
- Writing code → check `.pikb/CONVENTIONS.md`
- Multi-module changes → check `.pikb/MAP.md`
- Error / risky edit → check `.pikb/PITFALLS.md` (and `.pi/kb/PITFALLS.md`)
- New repo → create `.pi/kb/CONTEXT.md`
- Significant change → ask: "knowledge base 需要更新吗?"

Search: `~/.agents/skills/lore/scripts/quick-ref.sh <keyword>`
Missing KB in a complex workspace → `/skill:lore 创建知识库`
